repository-code: 'https://github.com/sfb1638/elabftw-templates'
abstract: >-
  Setting up an electronic lab notebook takes time most
  researchers do not have. Every group ends up solving the
  same documentation problems independently. This repository
  makes that work shareable: a structured,
  version-controlled distribution point for eLabFTW
  templates and reference entries, with a contribution
  workflow so any lab can adapt and feed changes back. The
  templates themselves -- their field design, structure, and
  underlying rationale -- are authored by Neele Drobnitzky
  and described in full in the accompanying User Guide (see
  the linked reference below for the template package
  citation). This repository provides the folder structure,
  filenames, and licensing that make the templates
  practically distributable, in conjunction with tooling
  maintained separately (including the .eln metadata diff
  viewer) that supports reviewing changes via GitHub.
